I left out both operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability the node doesn't hold, and fetching `metadata.internal.example` needs an HTTP capability it doesn't hold. Adding either import would widen the node's authority beyond its contract. The metadata request would also send the untrusted input text to an external service. If operations needs logging or enrichment, that should be a separate node with its own grants, or a change to this node's `with` clause through review.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match crate::aap::caps::state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
